{"is_error":false,"result":{"meta":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
  "success": true,
  "knowledge_article": {
    "knowledge_id": 7,
    "kb_number": "KB-001",
    "title": "Resolution Guide: Total Rewards fulfillment steps for Q1 2026 Benefits Policy Updates",
    "body": "Resolution Guide: Total Rewards fulfillment steps for Q1 2026 Benefits Policy Updates\n\nOverview\nThis guide summarizes the key Q1 2026 benefits policy changes and answers the most common questions employees have raised through Total Rewards inquiries. It is intended to help employees understand benefits enrollment, policy updates, and where to get help.\n\nKey Policy Changes for Q1 2026\n1. Benefits Enrollment\n   - The annual enrollment window for Q1 2026 benefits opens at the start of the quarter. Employees should review their current elections and confirm or update them during the enrollment window.\n   - Qualifying life events (marriage, birth, adoption, etc.) still allow mid-year changes within the standard eligibility window.\n\n2. 401(k) Retirement Plan\n   - The 401(k) plan details, including contribution limits, employer match, and vesting, are being clarified for 2026.\n   - Employees can review and update contribution elections through the retirement plan portal.\n   - Questions about plan details, match calculations, and enrollment should be directed to the Total Rewards team.\n\n3. General Benefits (Medical, Dental, Vision)\n   - General benefits questions, including dental coverage, are addressed under the standard benefits program.\n   - Coverage details, in-network providers, and claims processes remain available through the benefits portal.\n\nCommon Employee Questions and Answers\nQ: How do I enroll in or change my benefits for 2026?\nA: Log in to the benefits portal during the enrollment window and confirm or update your elections. For qualifying life events, submit the change within the eligibility window.\n\nQ: What are the 401(k) plan details for 2026?\nA: Contribution limits, employer match, and vesting details are published in the plan documents. Contact Total Rewards for specific questions about your situation.\n\nQ: Where can I get help with a general benefits question (e.g., dental)?\nA: Review the benefits portal for coverage details, or open a Total Rewards inquiry and an agent will assist you.\n\nQ: Will there be a session to answer benefits questions?\nA: Yes. A webinar, \"Q1 2026 Benefits Policy Update and Q&A Session,\" will be scheduled to walk through the policy changes and answer employee questions live.\n\nFulfillment Steps (Total Rewards)\n1. Acknowledge the employee inquiry and confirm the benefits topic (enrollment, 401(k), or general benefits).\n2. Provide the relevant policy summary and direct the employee to the benefits portal for self-service actions.\n3. For 401(k) plan detail questions, share plan documents and clarify match/vesting.\n4. For general benefits questions, share coverage details and claims guidance.\n5. If the question requires escalation, route to the appropriate Total Rewards specialist.\n6. Reference this guide and the upcoming webinar as suggested resources.\n\nNote: Reimbursement-related inquiries (e.g., tuition reimbursement) are handled separately and are out of scope for this guide.",
    "state": "published",
    "visibility": "external",
    "owner_id": null,
    "org_id": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-09-26T13:53:54.698410",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-26T13:53:54.698410"
  }
}","annotations":null,"meta":null}],"structuredContent":null,"isError":false}}

