{"is_error":false,"result":{"meta":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
  "success": true,
  "knowledge_article": {
    "knowledge_id": 7,
    "kb_number": "KB-001",
    "title": "Resolution Guide: Total Rewards fulfillment steps for Q1 2026 Benefits Policy Updates",
    "body": "Resolution Guide: Total Rewards fulfillment steps for Q1 2026 Benefits Policy Updates\n\nPurpose\nThis guide summarizes the key Q1 2026 benefits policy changes and answers the most common questions employees have raised through Total Rewards benefits inquiries (general benefits and 401(k) plan questions).\n\nKey Policy Changes for Q1 2026\n1. Benefits Enrollment: The annual enrollment window and mid-year qualifying life event process have been updated. Employees should review their current elections and confirm dependents before the enrollment deadline.\n2. 401(k) Retirement Plan: Contribution limits and employer match details have been updated for the 2026 plan year. Review your contribution percentage and beneficiary designations.\n3. Dental and General Benefits: Coverage tiers, in-network provider guidance, and claim submission steps have been clarified.\n\nCommon Employee Questions and Answers\nQ: How do I confirm my 401(k) contribution and employer match for 2026?\nA: Log in to the benefits portal, open the 401(k) Retirement Plan section, and review your contribution percentage and match details. Update your elections if needed.\n\nQ: What do I need to do during the Q1 2026 benefits enrollment window?\nA: Review your current elections, verify dependents, and submit any changes before the enrollment deadline. Changes made outside the window require a qualifying life event.\n\nQ: How do I find in-network providers for dental and general benefits?\nA: Use the provider directory in the benefits portal and filter by your plan and network.\n\nQ: Where can I get help if my question isn't answered here?\nA: Attend the Q1 2026 Benefits Policy Update and Q&A Session webinar, or open a Total Rewards HR case.\n\nFulfillment Steps for Agents\n1. Identify whether the inquiry relates to general benefits, 401(k), or another Total Rewards topic.\n2. Share this resolution guide with the employee as a suggested resource.\n3. Confirm the employee's understanding and offer the upcoming webinar for additional clarity.\n4. Update the case work notes and close once the employee's question is resolved.",
    "state": "published",
    "visibility": "external",
    "owner_id": null,
